Subject: [PATCH] drm: mediatek: turner: latch the fetch address on every flip

The panel kept showing the first frame because the OEM writes the 34-bit
fetch address as a low word plus four high bits on every flip, and the
high write is what latches the new address. Also record the OEM DSI
output-buffer thresholds, the relay tick, and the scanout test pattern.

---
